    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p6_b25",
      "text": "Topology components and contribution analysis.\nWe\nregress normalized task success on topology features pooled\nacross tasks. Table 5 shows that cycle count and contra-\ndiction score have the largest negative coefficients, while\nminimal path coverage has a positive coefficient; raw graph\nsize is not statistically significant. These results indicate\nthat naive verbosity does not explain the observed gains.\nTo control for confounding, we also include semantic score\nand reference margin in the regression. Topology features\nremain significant under this model, although coefficients\nshrink, suggesting that structural information contributes\nbeyond semantics and difficulty. In practice, these find-\n",
